{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1234417-lady-lovelace","id":1234417,"title":"Lady Lovelace","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-12T15:03:42-07:00","id":1234417,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Lady Lovelace","content":"This is about something I came up with for my game last night. In the middle of a picnic, a dog ran up and ate the sandwich out of someone's hand. It was all good till the dog talked to them in a voice they heard not with their ears, nor with their mind, but in their heart. Long story short, this dog came to seek help (but got distracted) for it's owner who had been a terrible (and eventually fatal) accident. The owner was a changeling.<br /> <br /> What the players don't know/I think didn't notice was the dog could see through the Mask and they don't know WHY it can talk. Which brings me to the idea. What happens when an animal has a passion for a promise so pure that even the the Wyrd sits up and takes notice? What happens when the one they made the promise to is taken? My thoughts is, if the Wyrd did take notice (and I consider this a pretty rare thing for an already fairly rare event), they will be drawn into the Hedge. They will generally find their way to Arcadia, a place ruled by creatures who won't understand them. Not really. They are beings whose feelings were so pure that they were drawn past the Hedge, but these emotions are nothing that the Fae can sup upon for Glamour. These creatures are somewhat protected by the Wyrd and the fact they don't fit into the worldview the Fae created with Arcadia. Their presence is almost a bane... so they can lead the changeling home.<br /> <br /> But here's the thing... while they didn't fit the rules of Arcadia, passing back Ironside changes them. They are no longer the animal that left Earth, nor even the one that left Arcadia. They become a better vessel for the Wyrd, more human-like along with the powers common to all Avowed as well as the weaknesses the Avowed have. This means that all animals are now sentient, though they might still not be SMART for a human or even average. Mostly I made Lady Lovelace (the black lab dog of the story) as a normal character. The big differences are that I don't see an animal having Integrity, but something more tailored towards their origins and movement modifier isn't 5 (and might have movement choices like flight). Also, a lot of social merits aren't going to fit them because they're an animal, not a human.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I thought the concept was an interesting one, and I welcome other peoples' thoughts on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T21:18:20-07:00","id":1234530,"title":"","content":"I really like this idea!<br /> <br /> It might be helpful to use some Innocents rules on animal Avowed; their anchors are Asset and Fault, they have fewer skill points to throw around and there are some custom Merits that adult human characters don't have access to."